# ISpect integration patch

Upstream: [ispect 7.2.0](https://pub.dev/packages/ispect/versions/7.2.0), MIT.
Archive SHA-256: `811faa1ce8a1613a2376c528efee9e177aa89593e3c0e187c2516154a7b23935`.
`lib/`, `LICENSE` and `pubspec.yaml` are the published source, not a new viewer.

Local version: `7.2.0+alshamel.1`. Upstream monorepo-only dependency overrides
are omitted; dependencies resolve through the host workspace lockfile.
The complete functional delta is:

1. Export the existing `LogsScreen` for embedding through the package barrel.
2. Restore desktop log keyboard focus after search only while its own focus
   scope is active; never reclaim focus from a sibling application pane.
3. Handle the log-search global shortcut only while that same scope is active.

The host owns pane sizing, visibility and its nested Navigator. This patch does
not change capture, serialization, business requests, exports or logger state.
Regression evidence: `test/alshamel/services/windows_diagnostic_test.dart` in the
host package exercises the real viewer, focus transfer, hidden-pane exclusion,
resizing, RTL and preservation of the host route/draft.

When an upstream release exposes embedding and respects sibling focus scopes,
replace this path dependency with that release after the focused tests pass.
Removing Windows diagnostics removes this folder and its dependencies; no app
feature or domain model depends on it.
